{
  "dom_id": "step-q154868",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "If ${a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+6$ with ${a}_{1}=-3,$ then ${a}_{2}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+6\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}=-3.$\n\nWe compute ${a}_{2}$ by substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & ={a}_{n}+6 \\\\ {a}_{1+1} & ={a}_{1}+6 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+6 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =(-3)+6 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{2}=3.$",
